-- title:
--   Euler characteristic of section twists on a fibre subscheme
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $C$ a scheme and $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a separated morphism, and let $U \subseteq C$ be an open subscheme such that the composite of $U \hookrightarrow C$ with $c$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$. Let $\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_m$ be sections of $c$ over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ (morphisms $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ composing with $c$ to the identity), each with set-theoretic image contained in $U$, and let $\mathrm{pos},\mathrm{neg} : \{1,\dots,m\} \to \mathbb{N}$. Let $k$ be a field and $t : \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, write $P := C \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} k$, and let $I_j :=$ `sectionIdeal c (σ j) t`, the ideal sheaf data on $P$ cutting out the induced section $\sigma_{j,t}$. Let $J$ be ideal sheaf data on $P$ with closed subscheme $Y := J.\mathrm{subscheme}$ and let $y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper. Assume for each $j$ that the pullback ideal $I_j|_Y$ (comap along $Y \hookrightarrow P$) is invertible, i.e. every point of $Y$ has an affine basic open neighbourhood on which this ideal is generated by a single nonzerodivisor; that the closed subscheme of $I_j|_Y$ is finite over $\operatorname{Spec} k$ via $y$; and that its fibre rank at every point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ equals $r_j \in \mathbb{N}$. Let $\mathcal{W}$ be a two-chart affine cover of $Y$ (two affine opens with affine intersection whose union is $Y$). Put $L := \bigotimes_{j} \bigl((I_j^{\mathrm{pos}_j})^{\vee\text{-module}} \otimes (I_j^{\mathrm{neg}_j})\text{-module}\bigr)$, formed as the right fold over $j = 1,\dots,m$ of the tensor factors $\mathrm{sectionTwist}(c,\sigma_j,t,\mathrm{pos}_j) \otimes (I_j^{\mathrm{neg}_j}).\mathrm{module}$ starting from the unit module, and let $\chi_{\mathcal{W}}(M) := \dim_k H^0 - \dim_k H^1$ denote the difference of the $k$-dimensions of the kernel and the cokernel of the two-chart Čech differential of the sections of $M$ over $\mathcal{W}$ relative to $y$. Then $$\chi_{\mathcal{W}}(L|_Y) = \chi_{\mathcal{W}}(\mathcal{O}_Y) + \sum_{j=1}^{m} (\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j)\, r_j,$$ where $L|_Y$ is the pullback of $L$ along $Y \hookrightarrow P$ and $\mathcal{O}_Y$ is the unit module of $Y$.
--
--   This is the multidegree computation for a line bundle written as a divisor supported on sections: on a closed subscheme $Y$ of the fibre $C_t$, the Euler-characteristic degree of $\mathcal{O}(\sum_j (\mathrm{pos}_j - \mathrm{neg}_j)\sigma_j)$ exceeds that of $\mathcal{O}_Y$ by the signed count $\sum_j (\mathrm{pos}_j-\mathrm{neg}_j) r_j$ of the degrees with which the sections meet $Y$. It is used in the analysis of line bundles on resolved models of modular curves, via [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.eulerChar_sectionsOf_pullback_strictTransform_eq_of_multidegree_eq_zero_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.eulerChar_sectionsOf_pullback_strictTransform_eq_of_multidegree_eq_zero_of_surjective); the induction over the $m$ factors rests on the single-twist case [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsInvertible.eulerChar_sectionsOf_tensor_invModule_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.IsInvertible.eulerChar_sectionsOf_tensor_invModule_eq) together with invertibility of the ideals of the sections.
